diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index e5f2541..29ec3d0 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -14,6 +14,15 @@ project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).
 - `set_key` and `unset_key` no longer leave a `.tmp_*` file behind on Windows when writing a read-only `.env` fails, and the error raised is the one from the failed write rather than from cleaning up the temporary file by [@MohammedAlkindi] in [#686]
 - `load_dotenv`, `dotenv_values`, `get_key`, `set_key`, `unset_key` and the CLI `--file` option now expand a leading `~` to the user's home directory by [@veeceey] in [#615]
 - `find_dotenv` and the IPython `%dotenv` magic now expand a leading `~` in the file name by [@theskumar] in [#714]
+- `set_key`, `unset_key` and the CLI `set`/`unset` commands no longer convert the line endings of a `.env` file: reading and writing are done with `newline=""`, so a CRLF file keeps CRLF on every platform and a new line follows the terminator of its neighbours
+- `set_key` and `unset_key` no longer drop a leading UTF-8 BOM, and a carriage return inside a value now survives the write/read round-trip instead of being read back as `\n`
+- `dotenv list` and `dotenv get` decode the `.env` file as UTF-8, matching what `set_key` and `dotenv set` write, instead of following the process locale (GBK on Chinese Windows produced mojibake or a `UnicodeDecodeError`). An undecodable file now prints an error and exits with code 2 instead of raising a traceback
+- `set_key` now rejects a key it cannot write faithfully (one containing whitespace, `=`, `#`, a quote at either end, or the empty string) instead of writing a line that is read back as a different variable while reporting success
+- `dotenv_values` now uses the default in `${name:-default}` when the variable is set but empty (POSIX semantics); a value of `"0"` is still treated as a real value, not as empty
+- A bare `NAME` declaration no longer masks a real environment variable of the same name when a later value is expanded with `${NAME}`
+- `load_dotenv` now returns `False` for content holding only valueless declarations, matching its documented contract of returning `True` only when at least one variable was set
+- Parsing a CRLF stream after a malformed statement now consumes the whole `\r\n` instead of leaving the `\n` for the next binding, which shifted the line numbers of later warnings and made `set_key`/`unset_key` glue two lines together when a statement was removed
+- `parse_variables` is now linear instead of quadratic on an unterminated expansion: a value made of many `${` with no `}` used to take ~1.8 s for 16 KB and ~7.7 s for 32 KB
 
