+    # No terminator at the very end: use the last one that appears, which is
+    # the convention of the final complete line. Matching the alternatives in
+    # one pass is what keeps the "\n" of a CRLF pair from being read as a lone
+    # LF (searching for "\n" and "\r" separately does exactly that).
+    matches = _line_break.findall(text)
